it's now been over a year since apple  revealed the m1 imac at their spring  event it has been extremely useful to us  in our office since our main editor  angelic has been editing basically every  single video that you've seen come up on  our channel over the past year with the  24 inch imac but now we've recently  started to get a flood of leaks for the  upcoming m2 max that we're all expecting  to get sometime this year and  unfortunately the 24 inch imac has been  missing from those leaks but over the  past few days we finally got some major  leak and rumor confirmation of what all  of us feared it looks like there will be  no 24 inch m2 imac and apple is instead  going to be holding off until the m3  chip is ready to update this imac again  so in this video i'm going to be going  through all of those leaks and putting  all the little puzzle pieces together to  try to find out why apple would do this  as well as which features we should  expect and how much performance we  should expect as well and finally i'm  gonna answer a couple of the most  important questions when is it expected  to actually launch and should you wait  for it compared to just buying the  current m1 imac right now and before i  get into all those leaks i've got to  share our experience with the 24 inch m1  imac over the past year like i said  before our editor angelica has been  using it full time to edit almost all of  our youtube videos and she's been  absolutely loving it and that's pretty  impressive because she used to edit on a  27-inch imac from 2020 which was almost  two times more expensive than this new  m1 imac in fact she likes it so much  that she even said that she wishes she  had this imac at her house and she said  she's gotten used to the smaller display  size and has no issues at all and she  especially loves how much more snappy  the m1 chip is compared to the old intel  chips so with all that said it should  give us some perspective in terms of the  future 24 inch imac update because if  this current m1 model can already  satisfy the editing needs of a youtube  channel like ours which tries to post 6  videos per week it should be enough for  the vast majority of people but now  let's finally jump into the leaks and  rumors with a huge report from mark  german who was the most reliable apple  analyst out there this past sunday he  talked about what we should expect for  the next upcoming max including a bunch  of m2 based macs like the macbook air  the mac mini macbook pros and even the  mac pro but in terms of the imac he said  that he heard about an m3 version of  that desktop being already in the works  though he imagines it won't launch until  the end of next year at the earliest and  this leak is actually a huge deal  because it perfectly matches up to  information from another source leaks  apple pro he says that his sources  expect a bunch of m3 macs coming late  2023 including a new m3 mac mini a  macbook air and a macbook pro and that  is actually exactly when i'm personally  expecting the very first m3 max to  launch late 2023 and the reason for that  is because the m3 chip is rumored to be  based on tsmc's three nanometer chip  process and digi times recently reported  that tsmc will begin production of three  nanometer chips in the last quarter of  2022 with apple actually launching three  nanometer base products in 2023  like the m3 chip and the a17 chip for  iphones but even before that we were  getting reports back in november about  three nanometer mac and iphone chips  coming as soon as 2023 and we recently  got another report from digitimes that  tsmc is on track to begin three  nanometer chip production in the second  half of this year but as far as the m3  imac leaks apple pro actually said that  it'll launch in early 2024  a few months after the first m3 max  launch in the fall quarter of 2023 and  that actually makes perfect sense to me  because that's exactly what apple did  with the first m1 max they launched  three of them in november of 2020 and  then they waited about half a year until  launching the m1 imac so i think there's  a good chance they're going to be doing  that again but now let's finally answer  the big question why in the world would  apple skip the m2 imac and wait that  long until refreshing it again with the  m3 chip well i think the main reason is  because almost every m2 mac is expected  to come with a total redesign except the  imac for example we're expecting a full  redesign for the m2 mac mini becoming a  lot thinner than before showing how  powerful apple silicon truly is  then we also have the m2 macbook air  which will also be getting a full  redesign with a new thin chassis new  color options mac save 3 and a new  display with white bezels and probably a  notch and the only other machine left  would be the base m2 macbook pro which  is by far the most confusing because  apparently this one is not going to be  getting a full redesign but who knows  maybe it'll take on the 14-inch macbook  pro redesign we really don't know just  yet but the point that i'm making is  that what if the m2 chip isn't going to  be enough of a deal by itself to justify  a new product refresh so apple is  combining the m2 chip with a redesign to  make the new m2 max look like a great  upgrade but now let's move our focus  over to the 24 inch imac and why apple  would skip the m2 chip refresh and wait  for the m3 chat well of course this is  the only m1 mac that actually received a  full redesign last year and since it  already has its redesign what if giving  it the m2 chip wouldn't be enough of an  upgrade to make it worth it in the eyes  of consumers and especially youtubers  who are going to be reviewing it like us  and i can tell you right now the m2 chip  alone isn't going to be enough to make  it worth upgrading from the m1 24 inch  imac to a new m2 model unless apple  packs in a bunch of other new features  and that's because i honestly don't  think the m2 chip is going to be that  big of an upgrade seeing as i still  believe it's going to be slower than the  14 inch macbook pros m1 pro chip so if  you're wondering how the m2 chip will  compare here is a chart of the single  core performance considering two  different scenarios with the m2 chip  based on either the a15 or future a16  chip cores and as you can see the single  core performance is where you'll see the  biggest advantage for things like web  browsing however in terms of multi-core  the performance is still lacking  compared to the m1 pro chip and that's  mainly because the m2 is expected to  keep the same 8 core cpu layout as the  m1 already has 4 efficiency cores and 4  performance cores now in terms of  graphics performance that's where we'll  likely see a nice boost because the  cores will not only be getting faster  but apple will be adding two more gpu  cores to the m2 chip but yet again we're  still expecting the graphics performance  to also lag behind the m1 pro chip so  with that said it kind of makes sense  why apple would wait for the m3 chip  because that would finally be a big  enough performance and feature jump to  make it worth upgrading to that new m3  24 inch imac because i fully believe  that the m3 chip will outperform the m1  pro in every way and the reason i  believe this is because the m3 chip is  reportedly going to be based on tsmc's  brand new three nanometer technology  which should have a pretty huge leap  over the current 5 nanometer technology  which is used in the m1 chip the a15  chip and likely the new a16 chip going  into the upcoming iphone 14 models which  would technically be called tsmc's n4p  process which makes it sound like four  nanometer but in reality tsmc themselves  confirmed that it's actually five  nanometer plus plus plus so going from  that to true three nanometer will be a  huge jump in performance per watt and it  would allow the m3 chip to get a lot  more powerful without requiring better  cooling solutions now on top of that  leaks apple pro gave us some exclusive  information concerning the chip layout  we should be expecting for the m3 chip  apparently apple has two prototypes of  the m3 one with an 8 core cpu which is  unchanged from the m1 and m2 and then  the other prototype has a 10 core cpu  adding two more performance cores and  this actually matches up to my own  personal expectations because it makes  sense for apple to add more cores as  they switch to better processed nodes  from tsmc because the cores have  improved performance per watt allowing  them to run cooler than before so apple  can balance it out by adding more chorus  now leex apple pro actually suggests  that apple could use both prototypes  with the lower end 8 core cpu version  going into the macbook air and the 10  core going into the base macbook pro  finally making a difference in  performance between both macs and in my  opinion i fully expect both of these  prototype m3 chips to outperform the  current m1 pro chip because of the three  nanometer enhancements and that's  exactly why i think apple is waiting  until the m3 chip is ready to refresh  the imac again especially if apple  actually adds face id to the imac which  they considered doing for the m1 imac  but they ended up holding off so with  all that said i think the m3 imac is  gonna be a great upgrade but because it  might not launch until 2024  i think most people should honestly just  buy the current m1 imac right now or  wait for the new m2 max coming later  this year now if you disagree with me go  ahead and let me know down in the  comment section below but if you enjoyed  the video go ahead and click the circle  above to subscribe for more videos like  this one and definitely check out one of  those two right over there thanks for  watching and we'll see you in the next  video  [Music]

